{"id": "daa0ef65-a92f-4fb5-9c70-8ec306ea1e1d", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "Let me look into this. I'll check your Q Business application configuration in us-east-1, your IAM Identity Center setup, and verify against AWS documentation whether cross-region pairing between the two is actually supported or if it's a configuration constraint that would block chat.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_gVnda6d9llWXlKTtHD4TFH", "tool_name": "gather_context", "input": {"prompt": "{
  "task": "Diagnose whether a cross-region setup between an Amazon Q Business application (us-east-1) and an AWS IAM Identity Center organization instance (us-west-2) is causing end users to be unable to chat with the Q Business application.",
  "context": "Customer has a Q Business application in us-east-1, and their IAM Identity Center instance is an organization-level instance located in us-west-2. They suspect this cross-region relationship is the root cause of users not being able to chat (e.g. ChatSync failures or access denied in the UI). Need to determine: (1) whether AWS Q Business supports/requires the IAM Identity Center instance to be in the same region as the application, or whether cross-region is fine since Identity Center org instances are inherently global-ish; (2) if cross-region is fine, what else could be blocking chat (e.g. user/group not assigned/subscribed to the app, IAM Identity Center application not configured correctly, missing subscription, service role trust/permissions issues, application not ACTIVE).",
  "steps_suggested": [
    "Use verify_aws_claim to check AWS documentation for Q Business + IAM Identity Center region requirements - specifically whether the Identity Center instance region must match the Q Business application region, or whether only ONE Identity Center instance per AWS Organization is allowed (which may itself explain why they look 'mismatched' by region).",
    "List Q Business applications in us-east-1 for this account, describe the application found, and check its linked IdentityCenterInstanceArn / identityCenterApplicationArn and its status.",
    "Check IAM Identity Center instance(s) visible to the account (sso-admin / organizations) to confirm the instance ARN/region and compare against what the Q Business app references.",
    "Check whether users are assigned/subscribed to the Q Business application (ListSubscriptions or identity center application assignments) since this is a common chat-blocking cause independent of region.",
    "Report findings: whether cross-region is actually a valid/supported topology for Q Business + Identity Center, whether the specific app's Identity Center link is healthy, and surface any other concrete misconfiguration found (status, assignments, permissions) that would explain users not being able to chat."
  ],
  "resources": ["Amazon Q Business", "IAM Identity Center", "us-east-1", "us-west-2"],
  "criteria": "Determine root cause definitively if possible: either (a) cross-region is fine and something else is broken, or (b) cross-region actually is the issue and explain the specific mechanism (e.g. app shows DEGRADED status, Identity Center link broken). Cite AWS docs for any region-requirement claim."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Check Q Business app config and IAM Identity Center region requirements to diagnose chat failures."}], "created_at": null}

