{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"AWS IAM Identity Center enables account access and application use in multiple AWS Regions - AWS","context":"AWS IAM Identity Center is a service that helps manage access to AWS accounts and applications for workforces. It is now possible to replicate IAM Identity Center from the primary AWS Region to additional Regions of choice, enhancing user access resilience and enabling deployment of AWS applications in preferred Regions. This feature automatically replicates identities, entitlements, and other information from the primary Region to additional Regions. IAM Identity Center users can continue to access their AWS accounts using the already provisioned entitlements in the additional Regions during disruptions in the primary Region. AWS application administrators can deploy applications in additional Regions using the standard application deployment workflow and assign users to the application in that Region. IAM Identity Center multi-Region support is available in 17 commercial AWS Regions for organization instances connected to an external identity provider, such as Okta, and requires a multi-Region customer managed KMS key. Standard AWS KMS charges apply for storing and using CMKs. IAM Identity Center is provided at no additional cost. To learn more and get started, visit the IAM Identity Center product detail page and user guide","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/02/aws-iam-identity-center-multi-region-aws-account-access-and-application-deployment/"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"AWS IAM Identity Center supports one-click multi-Region option for new organization instances - AWS","context":"AWS IAM Identity Center has introduced a one-click option for enabling multi-Region support when creating a new organization instance. Previously, this process involved several steps such as creating a customer managed KMS key, configuring key policies, and manually adding Regions. Now, customers can choose from three instance configuration options: single-Region instance, multi-Region instance, or custom instance. The multi-Region instance option automatically creates a customer managed multi-Region KMS key and replicates the instance to an additional Region, ensuring resilient AWS account and application access. This feature is available in 17 commercial AWS Regions for organization instances of IAM Identity Center, with standard AWS KMS charges applying for the customer managed key. To get started, refer to the IAM Identity Center User Guide and the Using IAM Identity Center across multiple AWS Regions page. IAM Identity Center remains free of charge","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/08/aws-iam-identity-center-supports-one-click-multi-region-option-new-organization-instances/"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"AWS IAM Identity Center extends multi-Region support to Identity Center directory - AWS","context":"AWS IAM Identity Center now supports replicating instances that use the Identity Center directory to manage and authenticate their workforce to additional AWS Regions. This feature, which extends multi-Region support, allows for increased resilience and deployment flexibility. When enabled, IAM Identity Center automatically replicates identities, entitlements, and other information from the primary Region to additional Regions. IAM Identity Center multi-Region support is available in 17 commercial AWS Regions for organization instances of IAM Identity Center that are configured with a multi-Region customer managed KMS key. AWS application administrators can deploy applications in additional Regions using the standard application deployment workflow while IAM Identity Center is managed in the primary Region. This feature is provided at no additional cost, but standard AWS KMS charges apply for storing and using CMKs. To learn more about IAM Identity Center and get started, visit the product detail page and IAM Identity Center User Guide","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/07/aws-iam-identity-center-extends-multi-region-support-to-identity-center-directory/"},{"rank_order":4,"title":"AWS IAM Identity Center now supports cross-Region trusted identity propagation - AWS","context":"AWS IAM Identity Center now supports cross-Region trusted identity propagation, allowing users' identity context to be carried with their requests to AWS services in different AWS Regions. This feature provides greater flexibility in architecting and deploying workloads across Regions without compromising fine-grained access control or auditing capabilities. Previously, trusted identity propagation was limited to services within the same Region, requiring consolidation of services or broad IAM roles for access to services in other Regions. Cross-Region trusted identity propagation is available at no additional cost in all AWS Regions where IAM Identity Center is available. This feature enables granting access based on user identity and underlying group associations, while maintaining individual user access control and auditing capabilities","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/10/aws-iam-identity-center-cross-region-tip/"},{"rank_order":5,"title":"AWS IAM Identity Center extends multi-Region support to more AWS Regions - AWS","context":"AWS IAM Identity Center, a service that connects workforce identities to AWS and streamlines access management, now supports multi-Region replication in additional AWS Regions, including those in AWS GovCloud (US) and AWS China. Previously, multi-Region support was available only in commercial AWS Regions. This feature enhances the resilience of user access to AWS accounts and applications by automatically replicating identities, entitlements, and other information from the primary Region to additional Regions. Users can continue to access their AWS accounts using already provisioned entitlements in the additional Regions during disruptions in the primary Region. Multi-Region support is available for organization instances using an external identity provider or the IAM Identity Center directory as the identity source and requires a multi-Region customer managed KMS key. To enable multi-Region support, create a new instance or configure an existing instance with a multi-Region CMK in AWS KMS. Standard AWS KMS charges apply for storing and using CMKs, while IAM Identity Center remains free. Multi-Region support is available in various AWS Regions. For more information, visit the Using IAM Identity Center across multiple AWS Regions page and the list of AWS applications that support deployment in additional Regions","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/10/aws-iam-identity-center-extends-multi-region-support-to-more-aws-regions/"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Check AWS docs on single IAM Identity Center instance per organization", "parent_id": "369a9305-6b7b-47e1-8f0f-7414295f4e58"}
